{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117396-another-shartha-progenitor","id":117396,"title":"Another Shartha Progenitor?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-04-21T21:36:48-07:00","id":117396,"title":"Another Shartha Progenitor?","content":"Below are two excerpts from the Lodge of Cerberus and the Lodge of Garm from <i>Lodges: the Faithful</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lodge of Garm (pg. 53)</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The world has already been unmade once, when the Shadow tore free of the physical world and the Uratha became Forsaken. Garm-Ur, son of Fenris the Destroyer, has already fulfilled the vague prophecies spoken of his destiny. He slaughtered a god when the world was shattered, and drank the blood of a fallen deity. As Father Wolf weakened over time, spirits punctured wounds in the physical realm and set up petty kingdoms. Here it came to be that the twin sons of Destroyer Wolf came to war with each other. Cerberus would not abandon his tribes to the spirits as the world sickened. Garm believed his sibling to be sadly misguided, and took the hunt to the haven of his enemy. Here, as the world finally crumbled and split, the son of the Destroyer killed his prey: a god of ills, a progenitor of <i>shartha</i>. Such is the fury and fervor of Garm of the Secondborn. Even Father Wolf and the Firstborn pack had to band together to slay the Plague King and Grandmother Spinner. Garm the God-Killer claims his victory alone \u2014 success through dedication, duty and unyielding strength.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lodge of Cerberus (pg. 37)</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the last days of Pangaea, as Father Wolf sickened and the worlds turned sour, Gurfuros-Ur was alone. The Firstborn pack ran with Urfarah, doing their utmost to balance his weakness with their strength. The werewolves plotted the downfall of their sire, committing to his slaughter because he was no longer a fit alpha. Garm-Ur, twin to Gurfuros, abandoned the human tribes the two spirits watched over. Garm left all behind in order to hunt and slay the malignant spirit-god he believed responsible for the hellish chaos afflicting the tribes, and Garm was hunting still when the Fall came.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does anyone know what &quot;god of ills; a progenitor of <i>shartha</i>&quot; Garm killed and than drank? The write-up in the core <i>Werewolf</i> book only talks about the Lodge belonging to Garm and the rune marks they brandish and the origins of the Crow and Snake <i>shartha</i> presented in <i>Predators</i> are left up to the Storyteller.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The Man and the Beast are having an amiable picnic in that Savage\u2019s head. It\u2019s rather disturbing.&quot; <i>- Blood and Smoke: the Strix Chronicle, pg. 22</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/145-jsm3050","name":"JSM3050","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-23T11:53:12-07:00","id":118026,"title":"","content":"This sounds like the perfect opportunity for an enterprising Storyteller to make their own shartha or to answer the origin-story of another.<br /> Also: I don't know if there's an answer given in any book, so I imagine it's up to the Storyteller (probably on purpose).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S8EuNtxeJKwq4sKVVPe16_N0ylIashKpgfCCuA1UOM8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Promethean Homebrew.</a><br /> <br /> Yes, I made it the same way as a Promethean. No, the authorities haven't found me yet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","name":"Ben Quo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar685_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-16T00:29:22-07:00","id":170471,"title":"","content":"Let's see. It is probably a plot hook that's up the Storyteller to fill, but if we examine the existing Hosts I think we can find the most likely candidate.<br /> <br /> The &quot;canon&quot; Hosts so far are: Spider, Rat, Locust, Crow, Snake, Leech, Wolf, Fungus and Worm. Excluding the ones with a clear and less ambiguous creation myth, we have Crow, Snake, Leech, Wolf, Fungus and Worm. Among those, I'll personally pick Crow.<br /> <br /> Here's the reasons:<br /> <br /> - They are bringers of bad luck, discord and ruin, possibly fitting the &quot;god of ills&quot; bit<br /> - Since they feast on the fallen, it's reasonable for their progenitor to be a force behind the chaos of the latter days of Pangea<br /> - Crows are associated with the dead and the Halaku's write-up in Predators hint that they have indeed some powers over ghosts. This could be used to explain a part of the undead invasion Garm-Ur and Gurforos-Ur had to face.<br /> - It's just appropriate for a a wolf named Garm to kill a monster associated with an animal sacred to Odin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 06-16-2014, 05:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-16T04:49:17-07:00","id":170562,"title":"","content":"From Blasphemies:<br /> <br /> Other Hosts<br /> <br /> While the Azlu and Beshilu are potentially not the only Hosts present in this dark world, these shartha are the most populous. Other Hosts exist on the fringes of perception, and these shard-bearing monsters often have cabals of human devotees to protect them and give them power.<br /> <br /> One man \u2014 calling himself 'Stinger' \u2014 is said to be swollen with living bees, a human hive whose followers help him build honeycombs of dried skin that help him to \u201cpollinate\u201d the two worlds. Stories have also told of neighborhood Cat Hosts, feral strays that colonize abandoned houses and hunt spirits and Ridden (and even Forsaken) with the help of hypnotized locals. It\u2019s even said that there have been 'Ghost Hosts,' human shells who have been Claimed or gutted by legions of dead specters, whose only goal in this world is to destroy others and make more of their demised selves. The Forsaken do not expect such aberrations to exist, instead focusing on the known enemies. Such shortsightedness proves deadly in the end.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-16T05:24:56-07:00","id":170588,"title":"","content":"Sure, but those are only rumors (for now). While they are good to spark the immagination of the Storytellers (I've made my own version of the Bee Host after reading that sidebar), we can only speculate about their identity. The Cats are generally associated by the fandom to the Cat Shapechangers from <b>War Against the Pure </b>and the Ghosts are simply<i> odd, </i>thus I'd esitate to call them Host. Legions of specters sharing a single body, yes. Shartha, not so much.<br /> <br /> Generally speaking, the only Shartha we know &quot;for sure&quot; are the ones I've listed before, since we have stats and motives that define them clearly (relatively speaking, we're still talking about the NWoD). The Kha-Yaawk are the only exception but, in the brief paragraph about them in <b>Lodges: the Splintered, </b>it's made clear that the Leeches are a Host and how they operate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 06-16-2014, 11:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-16T08:22:12-07:00","id":170760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117396-another-shartha-progenitor?p=170588#post170588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, but those are only rumors (for now). While they are good to spark the immagination of the Storytellers (I've made my own version of the Bee Host after reading that sidebar), we can only speculate about their identity. The Cats are generally associated by the fandom to the Cat Shapechangers from <b>War Against the Pure </b>and the Ghosts are simply<i> odd, </i>thus I'd esitate to call them Host. Legions of specters sharing a single body, yes. Shartha, not so much.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fandom interpretation aside, both the Bee Host and the Cat Host have plausible alternative explanations in some areas of the U.K. - the founder of the Melissidae bloodline for the former and the Alien Big Cats for the latter.<br /> <br /> It doesn't help that werewolf culture seems to have a habit of defaulting to calling any weird creature that's not possessed a Host.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-16T10:24:53-07:00","id":170862,"title":"","content":"The cats actually sound more like the Host of the Clutter, from the Horror Recognition Guide. And the bee and ghost hosts might just be bee and ghost hosts. The Aegis Kai Doru claims part of their hatred against the werewolves and mages is due to them releasing, among others, the Mistress of Honey, a being whose body was home to a hive of bees. The conspiracy outdates the Melissidae by a few hundred, possibly thousand years.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-16-2014, 01:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-16T10:38:52-07:00","id":170872,"title":"","content":"I must say that I really like the idea of the Bee Hosts, and loved Cinder's version for them. Sure, there may be a vampiric bloodline which also works with bees, but the idea of a Bee Host is too cool to be seen as &quot;a mistaken interpretation&quot; IMO.<br /> <br /> Also, I think that the Crows could work really good as the &quot;god of ills&quot;. for both the reason presented above and that it may explain why so few is known about them- after all, if their progenitor wasn't killed by Father Wolf, and Father Wolf is the most central figure in the werewolf myth, than it may be the reason why a demon- god killed by a Secondborn would take such a lesser place in their mythology. After all, if Father Wolf was the one to kill the other progenitors, and the Firstborn didn't managed it while a Secondborn did, it may show the Firstborn as &quot;weak&quot;, and so their followers may prefer to forget it ever happened.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-17T03:47:54-07:00","id":171534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bc5wHtOpRwQ\" data-code=\"bc5wHtOpRwQ\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/bc5wHtOpRwQ/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> Thought this was relevant","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-17T10:08:27-07:00","id":171740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117396-another-shartha-progenitor?p=170562#post170562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It\u2019s even said that there have been 'Ghost Hosts,' human shells who have been Claimed or gutted by legions of dead specters, whose only goal in this world is to destroy others and make more of their demised selves.</div> </div> </div> </div>This really would sound like Geists to the uninformed...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-17T10:28:34-07:00","id":171756,"title":"","content":"Sin-Eaters are more like the claimed, I think. It seems the ghost hosts have more ghosts in them, which would be pretty scary in its own right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-17T22:56:07-07:00","id":172495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117396-another-shartha-progenitor?p=171756#post171756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sin-Eaters are more like the claimed, I think. It seems the ghost hosts have more ghosts in them, which would be pretty scary in its own right.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, the Uratha view Sin-Eaters as Claimed. The Storm Lords especially take a dim view of them in the <i>Idigam Chronicle</i> (I believe the quote from the sample write-up was &quot;Claimed by a ghost is still Claimed&quot; or something similar).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The Man and the Beast are having an amiable picnic in that Savage\u2019s head. It\u2019s rather disturbing.&quot; <i>- Blood and Smoke: the Strix Chronicle, pg. 22</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/145-jsm3050","name":"JSM3050","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}